Fillets: the OnSame end of a rounding where the face at the end turns
tangentially from the opposite face (a top plane running on into the torus
of a rounded rim) and the opposite contact runs past that face's edge
before the end (mitcad#236).

A convex corner's top edge rounded (a cylindrical corner of a tab, radius
1, rounded with 0.79) up to the vertex where the top plane turns
tangentially into the rim's torus and the corner's wall meets that torus:
the wall's contact reaches the wall's edge with the torus before the
vertex, the top's contact crosses the top's tangent edge with the torus
past the vertex. The bodies stored in the .f3d files cut the blend there
with the torus, from the wall's contact to the point where the top's
contact meets the tangent edge, and the top's edge with the torus runs on
to that point. OCCT failed at the corner ("bouchon non ecrit", then
"echec calcul intersection").

- Update (the curve-surface one, used by IntersUpdateOnSame): the
  opposite contact is a circle (a blend of a plane and a revolved face);
  it meets the torus only on its prolongation past the stripe's end,
  across the circle's parameter origin. The reframing put that point a
  period before the first parameter (after the last), and the point was
  then rejected as out of range. Where nothing else is found, such a
  point on the prolongation is now taken, nearest the end.
- PerformOneCorner, OnSame: the missing end of the prolonged edge (from
  the vertex to the opposite contact's end) was the intersection of the
  opposite face and the face at the end, which touch along that edge (no
  transversal intersection to follow). Where the faces are tangent along
  the edge and the contact's end lies on the edge's curve beyond the
  vertex, it is now the edge's own 3d curve and p-curves continued to that
  point (ChFi3d_ProlongTangentEdge); else the intersection as before.

Upstream: new.
